# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository, always.
#
# This project is edited from both Linux (the Jetson, where it runs) and Windows (over the SMB
# share). Without this, a file written by a Windows editor lands as CRLF, git on Linux then reports
# the whole file as modified, and a one-line change arrives as a diff touching every line. Four
# files were already in that state when the repo was created — LICENSE, ai/rag.py, config/rag.py
# and tests/test_audio.py — which is what prompted this.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.onnx    binary
*.wav     binary
*.bin     binary
*.ko      binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.tar.bz2 binary
